WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.690
Sleep is a basic necessity of life,
but even more important is breathing.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.890
When you sleep, air travels through your
nose and mouth, down the throat,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.690
and into your lungs.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.510
The narrowest part of the airway is at
the junction where the soft palate,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.970
the tongue, and the back of the throat
all compete for the same space.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.710
When you are awake, the muscles
are tight, keeping the airway open.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.670
But when you sleep, the same muscles
relax, causing the airway to narrow.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.690
As the air passes through the narrowed
opening, the uvula and the

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.290
surrounding tissues begin to vibrate,
causing a condition known as snoring.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.210
If the tongue continues to fall back,
it will cause the breathing to become

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.750
slowed or completely stopped.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.490
This is known as obstructive sleep apnea.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:57.450
Sleep apnea can cause fragmented sleep,
shorter lifespan, reduced quality

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.090
of life, and even death.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.030
A comfortable and effective option
for treating obstructive sleep apnea is

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:08.270
with a custom-made, removable sleep
appliance that a dentist trained in the

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.850
treatment of sleep apnea can provide.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.350
With the sleep appliance in place, the
lower jaw is prevented from falling

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.450
back, keeping the tongue forward
and the airway open.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:23.010
Often this will reduce or eliminate
snoring and sleep apnea, providing the

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.230
body with deep, restful sleep.
